# ============================================================
# Mise — what never enters the build context (Part 34, ADR 0033)
# ============================================================
# The first entry is the one that matters: .env holds DATABASE_URL,
# DIRECT_URL and AUTH_SECRET, and a Docker build context is copied
# wholesale into the daemon. Secrets reach the container through
# `fly secrets`, never through a layer.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.gitignore

node_modules
.next
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# 🔴 `tests/` AND `scripts/` STAY IN, AND THE FIRST BUILD PROVED WHY.
# Excluding tests/ looked free — nothing in production runs them. But
# `next build` type-checks everything tsconfig includes, which is `**/*.ts`,
# which is `scripts/sweep-test-tenants.ts`, which imports
# `../tests/support/sweep`. The build died at the type-check pass with a
# module-not-found on a file that exists perfectly well in the repository.
#
# Excluding source from a build context to save a few hundred kilobytes buys
# nothing and costs a failure that reads as a broken import. Only things that
# are not code come out.

docs
.claude
CLAUDE.md
CONTEXT.md
README.md

# Dead since Sprint 0 — the local Postgres that Neon replaced
# (CLAUDE.md lesson 2, ADR 0033 Consequence 6).
docker-compose.yml

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
